Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.6.1): team priority, team choices and the team's one attack
and block (rules 805.2, 805.3, 805.5 to 805.7, 805.10b, 805.10d).

Reason: until now teammates received priority one after the other in turn order, put their
triggered abilities on the stack and declared attackers and blockers one player at a time, and
each player's attack was checked alone. With this patch a team has priority (805.5: priority
passes to a teammate who has not passed since the team last acted, so the team passes only when
all its players have, and then the next team gets it); a team puts all the triggered abilities its
players control on the stack in one order, which the team's chooser picks (805.7, 805.2:
Game.getTeamChooser, the given player by default, named by the game type); players who act in turn
order at the start of the game do so team by team, the starting team first (805.3a mulligans,
805.3b opening-hand actions: Game.inTeamOrder); and the active team declares one combined attack
(805.10b) and the defending team one combined block (805.10d): each player declares for their own
creatures, a human player is asked again when a teammate changes the declaration, and the
restrictions and requirements are checked against the whole attack or block, a human player whose
creature breaks one declaring again. Every change applies only to players with teammates
(Game.getTeammates), so every other game type plays as before. Commander Duels' TwoHeadedGiant
game type (engine/src/main/java/com/commanderduels/TwoHeadedGiant.java) names the chooser.
Upstream: none yet; offered with the other Two-Headed Giant patches.
Remove when: XMage upstream implements shared team turns, or Two-Headed Giant is dropped.

